  "details": "- GHSA-7whj-cfh7-xgm4: regexp: add the upstream follow-ups of the Regexp#to_s\n  fix: do not look for an option prefix in UTF-16 and UTF-32 regexps, compile\n  the group only when its preprocessing keeps the regexp encoding, and set\n  $VERBOSE to nil while compiling it\n- This build also ships the fixes of els1 to els4 below:\n  - CVE-2026-93577, CVE-2026-97229: regexp: wrapped jump offsets in Onigmo\n  - CVE-2026-110264: regexp: out-of-bounds repeat stack access in Onigmo\n  - CVE-2026-132825: enc: one-byte heap buffer overflow in the case mapping of\n    the sharp s in ISO-8859-x and Windows-125x encodings\n  - GHSA-7x2q-68qv-6p8x: regexp: double free in character class intersections\n  - GHSA-pvgc-g7gj-pv6h: regexp: out-of-bounds read in case-insensitive\n    backreferences at the end of the string\n  - GHSA-wpqw-5qxg-m68r: regexp: out-of-bounds read in case-insensitive\n    matching, unchecked code point and byte escapes\n  - GHSA-87fm-7w84-j2px: string: integer overflow in the case conversion of\n    very long strings\n  - GHSA-7whj-cfh7-xgm4: regexp: out-of-bounds read in Regexp#to_s of UTF-16\n    regexps\n  - GHSA-3p8q-wmhx-vm2w: regexp: heap buffer overflow from an integer overflow\n    of the compiled program size",
